    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/pta-peshitta/1tim#1Tim.2.11",
      "source_sha256": "96791adac691af34",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "A woman should learn quietly, with complete submission."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/pta-peshitta/1tim#1Tim.3.3",
      "source_sha256": "20728640717aa8b4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "He must not be given to wine, and his hand must not be quick to strike. Instead, he should be gentle, not quarrelsome, and not a lover of money."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/pta-peshitta/1tim#1Tim.3.12",
      "source_sha256": "de731d5012cb0ad4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "Deacons should each be the husband of one wife and manage their children and households well."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/pta-peshitta/1tim#1Tim.5.25",
      "source_sha256": "387b6ed7c67eb77d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "Likewise, good deeds are evident, and those that are otherwise cannot remain hidden."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "scripture/pta-peshitta/1tim#1Tim.6.6",
      "source_sha256": "3cc285a658f2b645",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 5,
      "text": "For reverence for God, with contentment, is great gain for us."
    }
  ]
}
